{
  "title": "KEIT — Cluster Right-Sizing (Kepler + kube-state-metrics)",
  "tags": [
    "keit",
    "sustainability",
    "kepler",
    "rightsizing",
    "findings",
    "reusable"
  ],
  "editable": true,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "5m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-24h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
        },
        "definition": "label_values(kepler_container_joules_total, kubernetes_cluster)",
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "label": "Cluster",
        "name": "cluster",
        "query": "label_values(kepler_container_joules_total, kubernetes_cluster)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "type": "query"
      },
      {
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
        },
        "definition": "label_values(kepler_container_joules_total{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\"}, container_namespace)",
        "includeAll": true,
        "allValue": ".+",
        "multi": true,
        "label": "Namespace",
        "name": "namespace",
        "query": "label_values(kepler_container_joules_total{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\"}, container_namespace)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "type": "query"
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": 100,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "> ℹ️ **Reusable dashboard from KEIT** — see [github.com/aknostic/keit/grafana/dashboards](https://github.com/aknostic/keit/tree/main/grafana/dashboards) for the source and other reusable dashboards.\n\n## What workloads are heavy, and what is wildly over-provisioned?\n\nKepler on a VM is **estimating**, not measuring (typically labels 70% of energy as kernel/system). But its **relative pod rankings** are useful, and combined with kube-state-metrics, you get a real right-sizing tool.\n\n**How to read this dashboard:**\n- **Top consumers section** — averaged over the dashboard time range. A heavy pod and a heavy namespace are different questions: per-pod tells you what to right-size; per-namespace tells you who to talk to.\n- **Right-sizing candidates** — ranked by ABSOLUTE waste (e.g., 'pod X wastes 800 MiB of requested memory'), not by utilisation %. A small pod at 1% util wastes very little; a big pod at 30% util can waste GiBs. The actionable wins are at the top of the absolute list. CPU uses 24h averages to avoid misclassifying bursty CronJobs.\n- **No CPU request set** — these pods are scheduling-unstable AND invisible to Kepler's ratio-based attribution.\n- **7-day cumulative energy** — for capacity planning. Different question than instantaneous power: a pod with steady moderate energy can cost more over a week than one that briefly spikes high.\n\n⚠️ **Don't read this dashboard mechanically.** A low-utilisation pod might be a Postgres standby waiting for failover — it's doing its job. Right-sizing is a conversation, not a script.\n\n**Designed to be reusable**: drop into any cluster running Kepler + kube-state-metrics + cadvisor."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 101,
      "title": "Cluster energy overview",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Average instantaneous power draw for the whole cluster according to Kepler. Sane VMs are 50–500W per node, so a 3-node cluster usually lands 300–1500W.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "watt",
          "decimals": 0
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(kepler_node_platform_joules_total{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\"}[5m]))",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Cluster total power (avg over range)",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Fraction of cluster energy Kepler can attribute to specific pods (mode=dynamic). The rest is labeled 'kernel' and 'system' — unattributable VM overhead. On a VM, 12–30% pod-attribution is typical. Low number = Kepler limitations, not your workload.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 1,
          "max": 1,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.1
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.25
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 8
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(kepler_container_joules_total{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",mode=\"dynamic\",container_namespace!=\"kernel\",container_namespace!=\"system\"}[5m])) / sum(rate(kepler_container_joules_total{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",mode=\"dynamic\"}[5m]))",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "% energy attributable to pods (vs kernel/system)",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Active pods Kepler is measuring. Sudden drops mean pods were evicted or removed — useful as a sanity check after decommissioning a workload. Example: on 2026-05-15 this metric dropped from ~80 to ~53 when our team migrated GitLab off this cluster.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 8
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "count(count by (pod_name)(kepler_container_joules_total{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",mode=\"dynamic\",container_namespace!=\"kernel\",container_namespace!=\"system\"}))",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Pods measured by Kepler",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 102,
      "title": "Top consumers (Kepler-ranked)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Top 15 pods by average power over the dashboard time range. Kepler's relative rankings are useful even when absolute values are noisy on VMs: a pod ranked #1 IS your heaviest workload. Investigate the top 3 — are they right-sized for the work they do?",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "watt",
          "decimals": 3
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 14,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14
      },
      "id": 4,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "topk(15, avg_over_time(sum by (container_namespace, pod_name) (rate(kepler_container_joules_total{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",mode=\"dynamic\",container_namespace=~\"$namespace\",container_namespace!=\"kernel\",container_namespace!=\"system\"}[5m]))[$__range:5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{container_namespace}} / {{pod_name}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Top 15 pods by power (average over range, W)",
      "type": "barchart"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Same Kepler data aggregated by namespace. Different question than the per-pod chart above: which app/team uses the most? A namespace with many moderate pods (e.g. gitlab with its many runners + workers) can dominate this chart even when no single pod is in the per-pod top 15. Conversely, plausible has 1–2 heavy pods but a smaller namespace total. Both views complement each other — use per-pod for right-sizing, per-namespace for chargeback / team conversations.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "watt",
          "decimals": 2
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "id": 5,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "values": [
            "value",
            "percent"
          ]
        },
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "mean"
          ]
        },
        "pieType": "donut"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (container_namespace) (rate(kepler_container_joules_total{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",mode=\"dynamic\",container_namespace=~\"$namespace\",container_namespace!=\"kernel\",container_namespace!=\"system\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{container_namespace}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Power by namespace (average over range)",
      "type": "piechart"
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 103,
      "title": "Right-sizing candidates (the actionable section)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36
      },
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Top 15 CPU **waste** candidates — ranked by ABSOLUTE millicores wasted (request minus 24h-avg actual usage), not utilisation %. This surfaces big absolute wins like 'Envoy Gateway wasting 100m' rather than tiny pods at low utilisation. Util% column shown for context: a pod at 5% utilisation wastes more proportionally, but a pod at 30% util can still waste more in absolute terms if it has a huge request. Uses 24h average so a bursty CronJob with headroom isn't misclassified.\n\n⚠️ **Don't blindly cut**: a replica with low utilisation may need full capacity when promoted (Postgres standbys, Redis replicas, etc.). A pod waiting for failover is doing its job. Always check what the pod's role is before reducing requests.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "right"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Wasted (millicores)"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "none"
              },
              {
                "id": "decimals",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Util %"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "percent"
              },
              {
                "id": "decimals",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.cellOptions",
                "value": {
                  "type": "color-background",
                  "mode": "gradient"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "thresholds"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "thresholds",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "absolute",
                  "steps": [
                    {
                      "color": "red",
                      "value": null
                    },
                    {
                      "color": "yellow",
                      "value": 30
                    },
                    {
                      "color": "green",
                      "value": 60
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Namespace"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.align",
                "value": "left"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Pod"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.align",
                "value": "left"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37
      },
      "id": 6,
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true,
        "footer": {
          "show": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "topk(15, (sum by (namespace, pod) (kube_pod_container_resource_requests{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",resource=\"cpu\",namespace=~\"$namespace\"}) - sum by (namespace, pod) (avg_over_time(rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespace\",container!=\"\",container!=\"POD\"}[5m])[24h:5m]))) * 1000)",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (namespace, pod) (avg_over_time(rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespace\",container!=\"\",container!=\"POD\"}[5m])[24h:5m])) / sum by (namespace, pod) (kube_pod_container_resource_requests{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",resource=\"cpu\",namespace=~\"$namespace\"}) * 100",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "CPU waste — top 15 by absolute millicores wasted (24h avg)",
      "type": "table",
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "merge",
          "options": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time 1": true,
              "Time 2": true
            },
            "renameByName": {
              "namespace": "Namespace",
              "pod": "Pod",
              "Value #A": "Wasted (millicores)",
              "Value #B": "Util %"
            },
            "indexByName": {
              "namespace": 0,
              "pod": 1,
              "Value #A": 2,
              "Value #B": 3
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "filterByValue",
          "options": {
            "filters": [
              {
                "fieldName": "Wasted (millicores)",
                "config": {
                  "id": "greater",
                  "options": {
                    "value": 0
                  }
                }
              }
            ],
            "type": "include",
            "match": "all"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "sortBy",
          "options": {
            "fields": {},
            "sort": [
              {
                "field": "Wasted (millicores)",
                "desc": true
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Top 15 memory **waste** candidates — ranked by ABSOLUTE MiB wasted (request minus actual). Memory is usually the biggest win because requests bound the scheduler directly: 1 GiB requested but 50 MiB used means 950 MiB of node capacity is locked up for nothing. Util% column shown for context. Instantaneous usage; if a workload bursts to higher memory, the request might be justified.\n\n⚠️ **Don't blindly cut**: a replica with low utilisation may need full capacity when promoted (Postgres standbys, Redis replicas, etc.). A pod waiting for failover is doing its job. Always check what the pod's role is before reducing requests.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "right"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Wasted (MiB)"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "decmbytes"
              },
              {
                "id": "decimals",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Util %"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "percent"
              },
              {
                "id": "decimals",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.cellOptions",
                "value": {
                  "type": "color-background",
                  "mode": "gradient"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "thresholds"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "thresholds",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "absolute",
                  "steps": [
                    {
                      "color": "red",
                      "value": null
                    },
                    {
                      "color": "yellow",
                      "value": 30
                    },
                    {
                      "color": "green",
                      "value": 60
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Namespace"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.align",
                "value": "left"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Pod"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.align",
                "value": "left"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 37
      },
      "id": 7,
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true,
        "footer": {
          "show": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "topk(15, (sum by (namespace, pod) (kube_pod_container_resource_requests{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",resource=\"memory\",namespace=~\"$namespace\"}) - sum by (namespace, pod) (container_memory_working_set_bytes{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespace\",container!=\"\",container!=\"POD\"})) / 1024 / 1024)",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (namespace, pod) (container_memory_working_set_bytes{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespace\",container!=\"\",container!=\"POD\"}) / sum by (namespace, pod) (kube_pod_container_resource_requests{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",resource=\"memory\",namespace=~\"$namespace\"}) * 100",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Memory waste — top 15 by absolute MiB wasted",
      "type": "table",
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "merge",
          "options": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time 1": true,
              "Time 2": true
            },
            "renameByName": {
              "namespace": "Namespace",
              "pod": "Pod",
              "Value #A": "Wasted (MiB)",
              "Value #B": "Util %"
            },
            "indexByName": {
              "namespace": 0,
              "pod": 1,
              "Value #A": 2,
              "Value #B": 3
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "filterByValue",
          "options": {
            "filters": [
              {
                "fieldName": "Wasted (MiB)",
                "config": {
                  "id": "greater",
                  "options": {
                    "value": 0
                  }
                }
              }
            ],
            "type": "include",
            "match": "all"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "sortBy",
          "options": {
            "fields": {},
            "sort": [
              {
                "field": "Wasted (MiB)",
                "desc": true
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Pods using MORE CPU than requested (util > 100%). They're stealing CPU from neighbours and risk throttling or eviction under load. **Action: INCREASE their CPU requests** so the scheduler can plan for them. Common cause: someone copied a Helm chart's default and never tuned it. Note: extreme percentages (1000%+) usually mean a tiny request like 1m — bump to a sane number like 50m or 100m.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "right"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Util %"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "percent"
              },
              {
                "id": "decimals",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.cellOptions",
                "value": {
                  "type": "color-background",
                  "mode": "gradient"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "thresholds"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "thresholds",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "absolute",
                  "steps": [
                    {
                      "color": "green",
                      "value": null
                    },
                    {
                      "color": "yellow",
                      "value": 100
                    },
                    {
                      "color": "red",
                      "value": 200
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Namespace"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.align",
                "value": "left"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Pod"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.align",
                "value": "left"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 47
      },
      "id": 10,
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true,
        "footer": {
          "show": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "topk(15, sum by (namespace, pod) (avg_over_time(rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespace\",container!=\"\",container!=\"POD\"}[5m])[24h:5m])) / sum by (namespace, pod) (kube_pod_container_resource_requests{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",resource=\"cpu\",namespace=~\"$namespace\"}) * 100)",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "CPU UNDER-provisioned pods (util > 100%) — bump these requests up",
      "type": "table",
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true
            },
            "renameByName": {
              "namespace": "Namespace",
              "pod": "Pod",
              "Value": "Util %"
            },
            "indexByName": {
              "namespace": 0,
              "pod": 1,
              "Value": 2
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "filterByValue",
          "options": {
            "filters": [
              {
                "fieldName": "Util %",
                "config": {
                  "id": "greater",
                  "options": {
                    "value": 100
                  }
                }
              }
            ],
            "type": "include",
            "match": "all"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "sortBy",
          "options": {
            "fields": {},
            "sort": [
              {
                "field": "Util %",
                "desc": true
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Pods with NO CPU request set. They schedule on kernel-default priority — get evicted under pressure, may starve under load. Also invisible to Kepler's ratio-based attribution. Two reliability bugs in one.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 57
      },
      "id": 8,
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "topk(30, group by (namespace, pod, container) (kube_pod_container_info{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespace\"}) unless on (namespace, pod, container) group by (namespace, pod, container) (kube_pod_container_resource_requests{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",resource=\"cpu\"}))",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Containers without a CPU request set",
      "type": "table",
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true,
              "Value": true
            },
            "renameByName": {
              "namespace": "Namespace",
              "pod": "Pod",
              "container": "Container"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 104,
      "title": "7-day cumulative energy (for steady-state planning)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 67
      },
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Total ENERGY (watt-hours) consumed by each pod over the last 7 days. Different from 'instantaneous power' above: a pod averaging 5W for 7 days uses 5×168 = 840 Wh; a pod that briefly spiked to 50W for 1h uses only 50 Wh. This view is for capacity planning — 'what's my weekly energy bill per workload?' — and shows which pods cost the most over time, even if they don't appear high on the current-power chart.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "watth",
          "decimals": 1
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 14,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 68
      },
      "id": 9,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "topk(15, sum by (container_namespace, pod_name) (increase(kepler_container_joules_total{kubernetes_cluster=\"$cluster\",mode=\"dynamic\",container_namespace=~\"$namespace\",container_namespace!=\"kernel\",container_namespace!=\"system\"}[7d])) / 3600)",
          "legendFormat": "{{container_namespace}} / {{pod_name}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Top 15 pods by 7-day energy (Wh)",
      "type": "barchart"
    }
